"home_raid_intro": {
"cards": [{
"label": "3:14 AM",
"speaker": null,
"text": "Something woke you up. You lie still for a moment, cataloguing the sounds of the building. The boiler. A fox outside. Then: footsteps, not from the corridor. From inside.",
"type": "tension"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "Your flatmates are out this whole week, but someone's in the flat. Moving carefully, which is almost worse than if they were crashing around - it means they've done this before.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You grab the nearest thing to hand - which, for better or worse, is the torch you left by the bed after last week when the power went out. After what feels like an eternity, your bedroom door slowly opens. You swing and feel the crack more than you hear it. THe intruder reels, then jumps at you.",
"type": "tension"
}],
"id": "home_raid_intro",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "start_home_raid_combat"
}]
},
"intro": {
"cards": [{
"label": "Earlier tonight — Whitechapel",
"speaker": null,
"text": "Rent is due Friday. The job search has been exhausting and fruitless. You have forty quid left in your account. An old friend, Archie, said he might be able to help. So here you are, behind a chicken shop on Mile End Road at half ten on a Tuesday, while Archie holds a plastic Tesco bag with what looks like an opened Amazon box inside.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"image": "res://assets/events/intro/1.jpg",
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "The buyers arrive in a grey Vauxhall. Three of them. That's one more than Archie mentioned. He notices too - you can tell by the way he stops whistling.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"image": "res://assets/events/intro/2.jpg",
"label": "It goes wrong",
"speaker": null,
"text": "The one nearest to you produces a Stanley knife. His mate walks towards Arch and the bag. The third one just stands there, which is somehow worse. Archie says, very quietly: \"Yeah, okay.\"",
"type": "tension"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Alright chaps?\" he lifts the arm with the bag to wave, drawing everyone's eyes. You notice the other hand slip smoothly into his back pocket and pull something small out.",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "He doesn't even move his arm, just flicks his wrist in a practiced motion and whatever he was holding flies through the air. Only one of the thugs even clocks it, eyes tracing it as it lands harmlessly on the ground between him and his mates. It shatters. The air around the three men goes thick and syrupy. They slow. Not stop - but slow, like a video buffering. Archie wraps the Tesco bag handle around his hand and walks, briskly, to the exit of the alley.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Coming, or what?\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"image": "res://assets/events/intro/3.png",
"label": "Fifteen minutes later — a Wetherspoons",
"speaker": null,
"text": "Archie orders two pints and a portion of chips. You sit down opposite him. Neither of you say anything until the chips arrive.",
"type": "resolution"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"What the hell was that?\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Orichalchum. Time-type. Slows things down in a radius - maybe four, five seconds of real time bought, if you compress it right. Was my last one, actually, so cheers for that\". He raises his pint to the door, as though saluting the muggers.",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"Is that... magic?\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Nah\". He sips his pint, \"Well, almost. It's basically magic. Don't make a big deal out of it. It's just like any product-  some people source it, some people turn it into something useful, some people use it. In between all that, people like us can make a quid or two connecting them. If we're lucky.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Look. You need rent money. I need someone who isn't a liability. Come out with me tomorrow - I've still got the calc from tonight, and I need to move it properly. I'd feel better doing so with backup. You in?\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "You sigh, thinking about your bank balnace. \"Yeah.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Good. I'll text you in the morning. Don't do anything that ends you up in hospital before then.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"image": "res://assets/events/intro/4.png",
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "He finishes his pint and leaves. You sit with what's left of your pint, the chips, and the fact that your rent problem has somehow become a different problem entirely.",
"type": "narration"
}],
"id": "intro",
"on_complete": [{
"flag": "metArchie",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"op": "set_stage",
"value": "buyer_event"
}, {
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "phone"
}]
},
"james_meeting": {
"cards": [{
"label": "Two days later — Bermondsey",
"speaker": null,
"text": "The address Archie texted is a storage unit beside a halal supermarket. You find him leaning against the corrugated shutter, hands in pockets, looking like he's waiting for a bus he knows is going to be late.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "The man who opens the shutter is in his sixties. Glasses with one slightly bent arm, a cardigan that has seen things. He looks at the two of you over the rim of his lenses with the specific expression of someone whose time is being wasted — and who has decided, provisionally, to allow it.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"James. Cheers for this. This is — well, he's helping me out at the moment.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"Yes. I can see that. Come in, then. Don't touch anything.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "Inside: shelves of labelled jars, a workbench covered in instruments that look like someone crossed a chemistry set with an antique shop. It smells of copper and something you can't name.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You lean in toward a row of sealed jars. One of them contains something that shifts — not from the movement of the shelf, not from any air in the room. It moves, very slightly, as if it noticed you.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You glance up. James is watching you. His expression doesn't change, exactly. But something in it does.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"He's the best craftsman I know. Turns raw calc into — well, you've seen what the pearls do.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"Don't flatter me. I'm the only craftsman you know. There's a difference.\" He turns to Archie. \"I have an order I need moved, but lack the time to do it. I'll give you the next batch of pearls - at cost - if you pick up a supply run for me. Stratford, in 45 minutes.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Yeah, alright. What am I picking up?\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"Physics calc, forty units. The address will be on your phone by the time you're at Stratford station.\" He sets down the jar he's holding. \"Your associate stays here.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Right.\" He's already moving toward the door. \"Cheers, James. Back in a bit.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "The door closes. James stands in the silence for a moment, regarding you with the careful expression of a man who has decided to do something he hasn't fully justified to himself yet.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"I have a substantial order for time pearls. My usual assistant is indisposed. You'll do.\" A pause. \"I realise that isn't flattering. It isn't meant to be.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"I don't know how to make them.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"Evidently. That is why I am going to explain it to you, slowly, using small words. Even a reasonably attentive puppy could manage this. I'm trusting you to clear that bar.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": "Crafting: Time Pearl",
"speaker": null,
"text": "James walks you through it. Time orichalchum, compressed into a glass sphere under controlled conditions. The calc does most of the work - you're just the hands. The sphere seals itself when it's ready. Or it doesn't, and the calc disperses. That's it, really.",
"type": "craft"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"The quality of the pearl depends on how cleanly you compress it. Rushed work means the time effect is weak and will last perhaps a few seconds. Patient, careful work produces something that can freeze a situation for longer. You will, at first, be rushing it. That's fine. You'll improve. Probably.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"And do try your very best not to fuck it up. The calc isn't free.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"You know, Plato described orichalchum as the second most precious metal in Atlantis. Wrote about it in the Critias  - considered it almost mystical in nature.\" He pauses. \"You have absolutely no idea what the Critias is, do you.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "It isn't really a question. You don't answer it.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"It doesn't matter. The point is that people have understood what this material is for approximately two and a half thousand years, and we still have people like Archie picking up deliveries outside a Poundland in Stratford. Make of that what you will.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You spend two hours at the bench. Some of the pearls work. Some don't. James says nothing about the ones that don't, which is both surprising and a little unsettling.",
"type": "resolution"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You leave with a crafting kit, a basic understanding of time pearl compression, and the distinct impression that James noticed something - and has decided, for now, not to mention it.",
"type": "resolution"
}],
"id": "james_meeting",
"on_complete": [{
"item": "timePearl",
"op": "add_item",
"qty": 2
}, {
"flag": "metJames",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"flag": "craftingUnlocked",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"op": "add",
"path": "contacts.james.unlocked",
"value": true
}, {
"contact": "james",
"op": "relation",
"value": 10
}, {
"op": "set_stage",
"value": "archie_craft_chat"
}, {
"contact": "archie",
"kind": "archie_craft_chat",
"op": "queue_pending_message",
"text": "Oi — how'd it go with James? Come find me."
}, {
"op": "add",
"path": "world.archieChatUnlockDay",
"value": 1
}, {
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "phone"
}]
},
"james_motion": {
"cards": [{
"label": "Bermondsey — the storage unit",
"speaker": null,
"text": "James opens the door in what you're coming to recognise as his default expression: mild disappointment that the world continues to contain other people.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"You again.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"I wanted to ask if you'd be willing to teach me any other recipes. I've been practising. I'm better with the pearls now.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"I'm sure you are. Mediocrity tends to plateau early. What's in it for me?\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"If you've got more orders than you can handle, I could take the overflow. Or just do the grunt work - the basic stuff that takes your time without needing your skill.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "James looks at you for a long moment. He picks up a glass sphere from his bench, turns it over, sets it down again. This appears to be how he thinks.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"You are proposing to be my assistant.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"If that's how you want to frame it.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"I want to frame it accurately. You would not be a partner, a student, or a colleague. You would handle simple orders. I would retain all complex work. You would not advertise yourself as my associate.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"That's fine.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"Hm.\" Another pause. \"Enhancement powder. It's straightforward. Life orichalchum, compressed differently to the pearls - outward rather than inward. Rub a small amount on the skin before physical exertion. Temporarily accelerates the user's movement.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": "New recipe: Enhancement Powder",
"speaker": null,
"text": "The compression is different from pearls. You're squeezing the calc by pushing the vice handle until your hands hurt, then gently scraping it to collect the powder. The result is a fine iridescent dust. James demonstrates once. He expects you to manage after that.",
"type": "craft"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"Quality scales with skill, as always. Low-grade powder gives you an edge over the average Joe. Better quality powder could make a couch potato compete with Usain Bolt. I trust you understand the principle.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "James",
"text": "\"I'll send you work when I have overflow. Don't expect it to be glamorous. And don't be late.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You leave with the recipe and the firm sense that James considers this arrangement a concession rather than a collaboration. You suspect that won't change.",
"type": "resolution"
}],
"id": "james_motion",
"on_complete": [{
"flag": "jamesMotionEventSeen",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"flag": "enhancementUnlocked",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"contact": "james",
"op": "relation",
"value": 1
}, {
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "contacts"
}]
},
"kx_delay": {
"cards": [{
"label": "King's Cross",
"speaker": null,
"text": "The departures board changes its mind for the fourth time. Somewhere behind the barriers, a Tannoy voice apologises for something it clearly isn't sorry about.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"choices": [{
"effects": [{
"op": "lose_time_block"
}],
"label": "Wait it out",
"result_text": "You wait. Time passes the way it only does in stations — all of it, somehow, at once."
}, {
"effects": [{
"op": "add",
"path": "player.cash",
"value": -30
}],
"label": "Pay for a cab (£30)",
"result_text": "You pay. The driver has opinions about the Northern line. You did not ask for them."
}],
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "Everyone's on the King's Cross deal. You are, for once, one of the delayed rather than the delighted.",
"type": "choice"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "Either way, you get where you're going. King's Cross remains, structurally, on its way somewhere else.",
"type": "resolution"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "kingscross",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "kx_delay",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"pigeon_omen": {
"cards": [{
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "A pigeon lands directly on your bag, considers you with the flat, ancient judgement pigeons reserve for people who look like they're up to something, and doesn't move.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You've heard the stories — fate-types collect near omens the way flies collect near anything else. You have no idea if this counts. The pigeon, notably, does not clarify.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "It flies off eventually, satisfied or bored, impossible to say which. You feel, absurdly, like your next piece of luck has already been decided somewhere above you.",
"type": "resolution"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "any",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "pigeon_omen",
"on_complete": [{
"flag": "luckyOmen",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"rain": {
"cards": [{
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "It starts raining the specific, personal way London rain does — not weather so much as a verdict. Nobody around you reacts; rain is not news here. You're soaked by the time you find shelter, mildly impressed at how quickly the city returns to pretending it didn't just do that.",
"type": "narration"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "any",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "rain",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"rival_prospector": {
"cards": [{
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "Someone else has clearly had the same idea about this patch of ground, and unlike you, they've brought company.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Rival",
"text": "\"Friendly notice. We're taking an interest in the good plot round here. A hundred quid says our interest fades. Your call.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"choices": [{
"effects": [{
"op": "add",
"path": "player.cash",
"value": -100
}],
"label": "Pay them off (£100)",
"result_text": "He pockets it without counting it, which is somehow more insulting than if he had. \"Pleasure doing business,\" he says, in the tone of a man who has never once meant that sentence."
}, {
"effects": [{
"op": "npc_claim_best_unclaimed_site"
}],
"label": "Let them have it",
"result_text": "You shrug and walk off. By the time you're back, someone else's flag is already in the ground on the best plot going."
}],
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "He says \"friendly\" the way people say it right before it stops being true.",
"type": "choice"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "London rewards neither generosity nor spite. It just carries on.",
"type": "resolution"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "any",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"requireUnclaimedSiteInDistrict": true,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "rival_prospector",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"roman_brick": {
"cards": [{
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "Half-buried in the churned ground of wherever you're standing is a brick — old, red, unmistakably Roman — in a spot with no plausible Roman history whatsoever.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You've seen one of these before. You didn't think anything of it then either. That's probably the point.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "You leave it where it is. Whatever's underneath London doesn't need your help finding daylight.",
"type": "resolution"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "any",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "roman_brick",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "add",
"path": "flags.oddities",
"value": 1
}, {
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"shoreditch_archie": {
"cards": [{
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "Archie appears the way he always does - already mid-sentence, as though the conversation started before you arrived and you're just catching up.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"Hello hello. Fancy seeing you here. You look like someone currently doing something mildly reckless. Carry on. I'm not your mum.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "You",
"text": "\"Comforting.\"",
"type": "speaker"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": "Archie",
"text": "\"I do try.\" He nods once, like that's the whole conversation, and drifts back into whatever he was doing before he clocked you.",
"type": "speaker"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "any",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "shoreditch_archie",
"on_complete": [{
"contact": "archie",
"op": "relation",
"value": 2
}, {
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"soho_tout": {
"cards": [{
"label": "Soho",
"speaker": null,
"text": "A man with a laminated card and the unkillable optimism of the professionally rejected steps into your path. \"Members' bar, love — and word is there's a proper market coming to Soho too. Ore, gear, all sorts. Not yet, but soon. You'll want to be first.\" He's gone before you can ask what \"soon\" means in Soho years.",
"type": "narration"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "soho",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "soho_tout",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"vein_raid": {
"cards": [{
"label": "Night work",
"speaker": null,
"text": "Whoever's sitting on this vein hasn't put a name to it, but the ground still belongs to someone. You case the approach twice. No obvious watchers. That's not the same as no watchers.",
"type": "tension"
}, {
"choices": [{
"effects": [{
"consumable_bonus": 0.05,
"on_caught": [{
"flag": "raidCaught",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"op": "notify",
"text": "Something moves that shouldn't. You've been seen."
}, {
"guards": 1,
"op": "start_raid_combat",
"template": "veinGuard"
}],
"on_success": [{
"flag": "raidCaught",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": false
}, {
"op": "notify",
"text": "No alarms. You're in clean."
}],
"op": "stealth_check"
}],
"label": "Go slow",
"result_text": "You take it slow — weight off every floorboard, timing the dark between passes."
}, {
"effects": [{
"consumable_bonus": -0.05,
"on_caught": [{
"flag": "raidCaught",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": true
}, {
"op": "notify",
"text": "Something moves that shouldn't. You've been seen."
}, {
"guards": 1,
"op": "start_raid_combat",
"template": "veinGuard"
}],
"on_success": [{
"flag": "raidCaught",
"op": "set_flag",
"value": false
}, {
"op": "notify",
"text": "No alarms. You're in clean."
}],
"op": "stealth_check"
}],
"label": "Go fast",
"result_text": "You go in fast. Hesitation is what gets people caught, or so you tell yourself."
}],
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "One way in. You commit or you don't.",
"type": "choice"
}, {
"choices": [{
"effects": [{
"op": "claim_raid_vein"
}],
"label": "Claim it",
"result_text": "You take it outright. Word gets round fast — it always does — and the relationship with whoever ran this patch takes the hit that comes with being seen to do it."
}, {
"effects": [{
"op": "loot_raid_vein"
}],
"label": "Loot and leave",
"result_text": "You take what you can carry and leave the rest where it stands. Someone else's problem, still."
}],
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "The vein's yours to deal with, however you got here.",
"type": "choice"
}],
"id": "vein_raid",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
},
"whitechapel_grief": {
"cards": [{
"label": "Whitechapel",
"speaker": null,
"text": "Whitechapel keeps its grief the way other places keep street furniture — permanent, load-bearing, mostly ignored. You feel it anyway, a low hum under the emotion-type in your bag.",
"type": "narration"
}, {
"label": null,
"speaker": null,
"text": "It passes, the way all inherited grief eventually does — not gone, just filed. The emotion-type in your bag sits heavier when you stand up, like it's been listening the whole time.",
"type": "resolution"
}],
"deck": {
"barometerState": null,
"district": "whitechapel",
"excludeIfFlag": null,
"weight": 1
},
"id": "whitechapel_grief",
"on_complete": [{
"op": "add_ore",
"qty": 1,
"type": "emotion"
}, {
"op": "set_screen",
"screen": "map"
}]
}
},
"FACTIONS": {
"collective": {
"colour": "#3a7a52",
"conquerThreshold": -40,
"description": "A decentralised network of vein finders and small traders. No hierarchy — or at least, no admitted hierarchy. Strong in East and South London. They find and protect veins collaboratively, share yields, and move ore through trusted contacts. Low entry bar, low ceiling.",
"id": "collective",
"industries": ["sourcing", "trading"],
"joinRelation": 25,
"name": "The Collective",
"raidStealth": 0.35,
"raidThreshold": -40,
"resourceLevel": 1,
"securityBias": -2,
"shortName": "Collective",
"startingResources": 200,
"tagline": "Community-run. Loosely organised. Surprisingly effective."
},
"conclave": {
"colour": "#2a8fc4",
"conquerThreshold": -20,
"description": "Old enough to have advised governments. New enough to use WhatsApp. The Conclave operates at the intersection of orichalchum and institutional power — they shape economic and political conditions that affect everyone else. Joining requires high standing, rare resources, and the willingness to do things that don't appear on any list.",
"id": "conclave",
"industries": ["influence", "sourcing", "crafting"],
"joinRelation": 60,
"name": "The Conclave",
"raidStealth": 0.65,
"raidThreshold": -20,
"resourceLevel": 3,
"securityBias": 3,
"shortName": "Conclave",
"startingResources": 1200,
"tagline": "Policy, pressure, and things that can't be admitted in public."
},
"firm": {
"colour": "#9b2335",
"conquerThreshold": 0,
"description": "A well-established crew with roots going back further than anyone admits. Operate across South and West London. Specialise in acquiring high-value veins by force and reselling refined product at premium rates. Professional, ruthless, not interested in small operators — unless you show promise.",
"id": "firm",
"industries": ["raiding", "trading"],
"joinRelation": 35,
"name": "The Firm",
"raidStealth": 0.55,
"raidThreshold": 0,
"resourceLevel": 2,
"securityBias": 1,
"shortName": "Firm",
"startingResources": 500,
"tagline": "Old money, new methods."
},
"guild": {
"colour": "#7b68ee",
"conquerThreshold": -30,
"description": "Formal, ancient, and deeply unimpressed by everyone. The Guild controls the majority of high-end crafting knowledge in London. James is a member, though he'd describe his relationship with them as 'complicated'. Joining requires demonstrated crafting ability and a sponsor.",
"id": "guild",
"industries": ["crafting", "trading"],
"joinRelation": 40,
"name": "The Guild of Applied Alchemists",
"raidStealth": 0.3,
"raidThreshold": -30,
"resourceLevel": 2,
"securityBias": 1,
"shortName": "The Guild",
"startingResources": 900,
"tagline": "They've been here since before the word 'orichalchum' was anglicised."
},
"network": {
"colour": "#1f9e96",
"conquerThreshold": -20,
"description": "No one's quite sure who runs The Network or what they actually want. They surface occasionally to broker information — who has what vein, who is selling, what the barometer is doing. They seem to know things before they happen. They are interested in you, which should be flattering and is mostly unsettling.",
"id": "network",
"industries": ["trading", "influence"],
"joinRelation": 30,
"name": "The Network",
"raidStealth": 0.8,
"raidThreshold": -20,
"resourceLevel": 2,
"securityBias": -1,
"shortName": "Network",
"startingResources": 500,
"tagline": "Information is the resource."
}
},
